    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on aggressive base-running and high-ceiling platoon matchups. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) stands as the marquee play of the day; his top-tier score is anchored by a favorable matchup against Flaherty and a +14% boost from a dynamic platoon advantage, making him our most critical asset for chasing scarce stolen bases. **Yordan Alvarez** (78.29) follows closely behind, with his elite xwOBA of 0.476 against Junk allowing him to transcend standard park factors. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** (74.27) remains a mandatory start; despite the challenge posed by Peralta, his role at the top of the order and a massive +13% platoon efficiency boost keep his floor well above the 60-point threshold for strong starts.\n\nWhile the depth of our lineup is robust, we faced a difficult decision at the margins. **Chase Meidroth** (32.38) was the only bench piece to warrant serious consideration, but his pairing against deGrom effectively cratered his projection. The high-skill profile of the opposing starter, combined with **Chase Meidroth**\u2019s placement at the bottom of the order, resulted in a sub-40 score that forced us to prioritize the overall efficiency of our starting nine. We continue to monitor the status of **Hyeseong Kim**, **Carson Benge**, and **Nelson Velazquez**, who remain inactive, while **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** are currently sidelined from the daily look.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the risks inherent in today\u2019s matchups. While **Junior Caminero** (55.19) and **Kyle Schwarber** (58.63) both hover near the \"Strong\" start designation, they are facing Cease and Sheehan, respectively\u2014two pitchers with high-tier stuff that tempers our expectations. **Dillon Dingler** (47.98) remains our most volatile start of the day; he occupies a marginal spot in the lineup, and his efficiency is dragged down significantly by a -15% dynamic platoon penalty. Owners should monitor weather reports, though our projections currently account for park-adjusted park factors; ensure no late-breaking lineup scratches jeopardize the efficiency gains provided by the likes of **Colt Keith**, **Trea Turner**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Casey Schmitt**.",
